          "encoder_s": 0.31977,
          "errors": 0,
          "words": 24,
          "native": false,
          "fallback": true,
          "native_requested": false,
          "hypothesis": "Stephen, leaning back and drawing idly on his scribbler, listened to the talk about him, which Heron checked from time to time by saying,"
        },
        {
          "id": "1089-134686-0018",
          "flac_sha256": "b8a5a3b85bee6bb8464083ed10da866d2a23be38a602e79c5de7362bddf992d6",
          "audio_s": 15.72,
          "wall_s": 0.7374749332666397,
          "cpu_s": 4.5027120000000105,
          "encoder_s": 0.34572,
          "errors": 0,
          "words": 41,
          "native": false,
          "fallback": true,
          "native_requested": false,
          "hypothesis": "It was strange, too, that he found an arid pleasure in following up to the end, the rigid lines of the doctrines of the church, and penetrating into obscure silences only to hear and feel the more deeply his own condemnation."
        },
        {
          "id": "1089-134686-0019",
          "flac_sha256": "dde10b08d59f3dfa89a9b8731ffb0b39da00ac2b5b23115c2700ea312d5ff8cf",
          "audio_s": 13.895,
          "wall_s": 0.8050262960605323,
          "cpu_s": 4.916342000000025,
          "encoder_s": 0.4019,
          "errors": 1,
          "words": 39,
          "native": false,
          "fallback": true,
          "native_requested": false,
          "hypothesis": "The sentence of St. James, which says that he, who offends against one commandment, becomes guilty of all, had seemed to him first a swollen phrase, until he had begun to grope in the darkness of his own state."
        }
      ],
